44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the meaning of the name of the constellation Cygnus?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cygnus is Latin for swan. Its bright stars also form the Northern Cross, a prominent asterism.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7285-adf3-7c7184374b19","description":"Swan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7fb7-b388-2c3cbf7ada6a","description":"Ring","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-79be-95b2-c90e4fc6269a","description":"River","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7a77-97c1-a8205f579ba4","description":"Mountain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7a8a-9c78-83c9c606f067","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"Although the Poodle is widely associated with France, in which country is it believed to have originated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Poodle\u2019s name is linked to the word \u201cPudel,\u201d referring to splashing in water; the breed was developed as a water retriever.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7156-a765-43a358169d4f","description":"Germany","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-74be-b69b-5e134d55ae4c","description":"Egypt","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7871-921f-dba2ffeac35d","description":"India","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7b5d-a56e-0e064f5cb3dd","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7107-b862-6b5828503648","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was built by CERN near Geneva?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"CERN\u2019s Large Hadron Collider lies beneath the French-Swiss border and lets scientists study matter through high-energy collisions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7ae5-9824-8a71d7b9fc5e","description":"Particle accelerator","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7ea9-b03e-aa6c9741923f","description":"Art museum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7643-b235-f32b3a1e2943","description":"Colossus computer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7bd2-baf2-b83367c6ab3a","description":"Rocket launch pad","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7926-9c93-3b015b58083a","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What was Rubik\'s Cube originally called when Ern\u0151 Rubik invented it in 1974?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Magic Cube was developed as a teaching tool for three-dimensional geometry before it was marketed internationally under Rubik\u2019s name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7a1f-87b6-f714d513a32d","description":"Magic Cube","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7a02-b5b1-ed216ec696eb","description":"Wonder Cube","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-749b-bf61-04eb28eefd44","description":"Hungarian Box","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7866-a670-cedd3e9b0cfd","description":"Colour Block","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7d8d-87ba-ba431d742c1d","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"According to the biblical story of Cain and Abel, what type of animals did Abel offer as a sacrifice to God?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Genesis says Abel brought the firstborn of his flock as an offering, identifying the animals as sheep.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-741d-8577-f75934baa708","description":"Sheep","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7d53-8744-33f384c39591","description":"Cows","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-718d-9afa-5b18f9d8b202","description":"Pigs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-70c5-8d9c-2b975a892ca9","description":"Chickens","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7ef5-bbbf-554958dca0b7","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What metal corresponds to the Spanish term \"plata\"?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Spanish word plata means silver; the element\u2019s chemical symbol, Ag, comes from the Latin argentum.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-724c-baf7-bba50f574f15","description":"Silver","correc