One Hundred and One Dalmatians gives 101; subtracting Snow White\'s seven dwarfs leaves 94.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-74bb-8d54-5b1737513495","description":"94","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7722-b187-5d79a3104233","description":"97","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7842-b568-2f0273bb60c8","description":"89","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7279-9a9c-a5d6c92f6fc5","description":"91","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7312-ae17-fe5fd5bc06aa","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What type of structures are used to conduct a water stream across a valley?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Aqueducts often relied on gravity to move water, and their elevated arches let channels cross valleys without following the terrain.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7d18-ae90-a96b5fd0431b","description":"Aqueducts","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-76f0-aef7-5ae4c593bd3e","description":"Canals","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7b1d-ade6-cafb76b65921","description":"Pipelines","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-785f-93c4-486d731a30a7","description":"Trenches","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-71ce-aeeb-a03d25efb87a","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the Latin term for \"the arm\"?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bracchium is the source of the anatomical adjective brachial, as in the brachial artery.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-72e6-8758-a73d9ff806fc","description":"Bracchium","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-75d4-9599-d7db0b0c094f","description":"Caput","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7f32-ac5f-39d0aabbac23","description":"Pedis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7c0a-a8fe-51d6af44f121","description":"Oculus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7571-8da3-73427cac5e12","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"What is the troy system of weights used to measure?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The troy system is used to measure precious metals. A troy ounce is about 31.1 grams, compared with about 28.35 grams for the everyday avoirdupois ounce.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-754c-a7ce-381b18098c9f","description":"Precious metals","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7685-b868-5bb3ffa693f8","description":"Radiation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-763a-ba84-0db6bc64c867","description":"Grain harvests","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7e48-9ce2-a6c074cfadae","description":"Liquid fuels","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-71a3-812a-d604841b4e74","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"In January 2018, which retail chain that kids love announced it would close about 180 stores?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Toys \"R\" Us announced the closures as part of a restructuring after filing for bankruptcy in 2017.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7915-bc8c-062c7f7ef407","description":"Toys \"R\" Us","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7405-b16c-3f6f9b3040b3","description":"Target","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7572-8518-ad1628f3d857","description":"Walmart","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7a7b-8a6f-b74d8623b970","description":"Amazon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-76d6-a53f-b21fad9bcbfa","category":"01a21312-b489-7095-8a30-44480fe2c4f5","question":"On which date is the Feast of St. Nicholas celebrated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Feast of St. Nicholas is celebrated on December 6. St. Nicholas was a 4th-century bishop of Myra whose generosity helped inspire the gift-giving figure of Santa Claus.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7c28-a024-630003dce5d4","description":"December 6","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-7841-adc4-05b8a5d04220","description":"December 18","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad11-75d7-9e29-6a0f95e57c4f","description":"December 25","correct_answ